From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:54:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20the=20first=20event=20loop:=20test=20app?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=86=92=20interaction=20page=20=E2=86=92=20receipt?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Opening a test app the person picked in settings now runs one closed loop:
the accessibility service hands window events to LoopRuntime, which waits
350 ms, re-reads the real foreground package (package name only), and lets
a pure-Kotlin LoopEngine decide. A new visit that passes the local rules
(enabled, screen on, unlocked, DSH not busy, no page open, cooldown) opens
an event and shows InteractionActivity in its own task; every way out
(Back button, system back, leaving, timeout, not shown) closes the event
once and the receipt is written atomically to files/loop/state.json.

DSH itself, system UI, keyboards and permission/security pages never start
or end a visit, so returning from the page or a keyboard popping up cannot
loop. Open events left by a dead process close as ABANDONED on recovery.

Existing phone control is untouched apart from three hooks in
PhoneA11yService, a read-only PhonePrompts.busy(), the plugin registration
and the manifest entry. Docs in docs/loop/.

